/**
@mainpage Botanik

@brief @c libbotanik - greenhouse-control firmware for the Arduino OPTA PLC
       (STM32H747 dual-core ARM).

Botanik runs on the OPTA's application core (the **M7**), alongside the PLC program
on the coprocessor (the **M4**): the PLC drives the I/O and control loop, Botanik
adds the operator-facing layer - a serial terminal UI, logging, health monitoring,
and the shared-memory link that ties the two cores together. The C++11 library at
its core, `libbotanik`, is platform-agnostic; the same code builds as a Linux
simulator or for the OPTA hardware.

This documentation is organised into four parts:

- @subpage introduction - what Botanik is, how the firmware is layered
  (sketch / site / base library), and how to stand up a new project.
- @subpage manual - operating a running unit over its serial terminal: the pages,
  the shell, and (later) the wiring and PLC-side setup.
- @subpage library - the engineering reference: subsystems, key concepts, the
  architecture deep-dives, the build targets, and the test suites. The full API
  surface is in the **Namespaces** and **Classes** tabs.
- @subpage reference - the `gh_mlb41` greenhouse, the reference site that every
  example here is drawn from.
*/
